AB  - The dependence of early occurring minimal brain dysfunction on the standard of living was tested. 1355 6 to 15 yr old patients with psychosomatic and psychiatric disorders were examined and divided into 3 groups: 'no brain dysfunction', 'suspected brain dysfunction' and 'brain dysfunction'. A highly significant correlation between brain dysfunction and a low socioeconomic status, evaluated in terms of living conditions and the father's occupation, was found.
